<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oichi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1547">1547</a>–<a href="/years/1583">1583</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Oichi no Kata</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Oichi was a younger sister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oda-nobunaga">Oda Nobunaga</a>, married to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azai-nagamasa">Azai Nagamasa</a> around 1567 to secure their alliance. After Nobunaga destroyed the Azai in 1573 she returned to the Oda with her three daughters, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-felix-de-souza">Chacha</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ohatsu">Ohatsu</a> and Go. She later married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shibata-katsuie">Shibata Katsuie</a> and died with him when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a> besieged Kitanoshō castle in 1583.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oichi.jpg" alt="Oichi" width="320" height="443" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 不詳 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Oichinokata.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
